---
description: Domain concepts and core rules of "Domov na varno", shared by the library and the server.
---

***definitions***

- :DemoValue: is a clinical number of this project - a curve value, a tolerance, a threshold - that is not clinically validated.

- :RiskTier: is `HIGH`, `MEDIUM` or `LOW`; the check-in schedule, duration, pain tolerance and silence thresholds of each are in [resources/risk-tiers.yaml](resources/risk-tiers.yaml), all :DemoValue: items.

- :Protocol: is a monitoring protocol for one kind of procedure, as [resources/protocol.schema.json](resources/protocol.schema.json) describes it, with `checkInSchedule`, `durationDays` and `painTolerance` added from its :RiskTier:.

- :Symptom: is an entry of a :Protocol:'s `questions`, the daily check-in questions, known by its `id`, with a `kind`:
  - `RED_FLAG`: a symptom a `redFlags` entry of the :Protocol: names; `SYMPTOM`: any other symptom to tick; `MEASUREMENT`: a number to enter, in its `unit`.

- :RedFlag: is an entry of a :Protocol:'s `redFlags`: `{ id, symptom, severity, action, patterns? }`, where `symptom` is the id of a :Symptom: and `severity` is `CONTACT_DOCTOR` or `EMERGENCY`.
  - The message shown for an `EMERGENCY` :RedFlag: adds 112.

- :LocalDay: is a calendar date in the `Europe/Ljubljana` time zone, written `YYYY-MM-DD`.

- :Report: is a discharge report: `id`, `patientId`, `procedure`, `procedureDate` (a :LocalDay:), `medications[]`, `specialWarnings[]`, `restrictions[]`, `recommendations`, `doctorContactPhone`.

- :Patient: is `id`, `name`, `phone`, `dischargeDate` (a :LocalDay:), `protocolId`, `reportId`, `caregiverName?`, `preferredCheckInTime` (`HH:MM` in `Europe/Ljubljana`), `accessToken` (the magic-link token).

- :DayAfterDischarge: of a moment is the number of :LocalDay: items from a :Patient:'s `dischargeDate` to the :LocalDay: of that moment: the discharge day is 0, the next day 1.

- :Trend: is how a value changed since the previous check-in, as the patient tells it: `MUCH_BETTER`, `BETTER`, `SAME`, `WORSE` or `MUCH_WORSE`.

- :CheckIn: is a final, append-only daily check-in: `id`, `patientId`, `protocolVersion`, `dayAfterDischarge`, `timestamp`, `wellbeing` (1-5), `pain` (0-10), `symptoms[]` (ids of `RED_FLAG` and `SYMPTOM` :Symptom: items), `painTrend?` and `wellbeingTrend?` (:Trend: items), `measurements?` (a number for each `MEASUREMENT` :Symptom: id given, as `{ "weightKg": 82.4 }`), `temperatureC?`, `photoRef?`, `note?`, `filledBy` (`PATIENT` or `CAREGIVER`).

- :TriageStatus: is `GREEN`, `YELLOW` or `RED`, in rising severity.

- :Reason: is `{ text, ruleId }`: `ruleId` is `R0` to `R7` and `text` is Slovenian.

- :Assessment: is an append-only triage result: `id`, `patientId`, `checkInId?`, `status` (a :TriageStatus:), `reasons[]` (:Reason: items), `createdAt`.
  - An :Assessment: of silence has no `checkInId`.

- :Alert: is `id`, `assessmentId`, `recipientRole` (`NURSE` or `COORDINATOR`), `createdAt`, `acknowledgedAt?`, `escalatedAt?`.

- :CheckInSlot: is one check-in a :Patient: is due to make: `{ day, index, dueAt }`, `index` 1 or 2 within its day.

- :History: is the final :CheckIn: items of one :Patient: made before the one assessed.

***implementation reqs***

- :Implementation: keeps its pure core in `src/core/`: no I/O, no reading of the clock (`Date.now()`, `new Date()` without an argument), no randomness and no environment.
  - Every core function that needs the time takes `now` as an argument; every one that creates a record takes its id as an argument.

- :Implementation: keeps every user-facing string in `src/strings.sl.ts`, in Slovenian with its diacritics (č, š, ž), with no emoji, and every file in UTF-8.

- :Implementation: writes every moment as an ISO 8601 string with its offset, and computes :LocalDay: items in `Europe/Ljubljana` with `Intl`, daylight saving time included.

- :Implementation: keeps each protocol file it is given as `src/core/protocols/<id>.json`, byte for byte, imported as a JSON module, and the :RiskTier: settings as a typed constant in `src/core/riskTiers.ts`.
